      "claim": "Mosliciguat, an acidic high-molecular-weight drug with low passive-permeability liabilities, had absolute oral bioavailability of 23.1% (dose-adjusted AUC ratio 0.231, 90% CI 0.199–0.269), supporting F ≥ 20% for similar acidic molecules.",
      "card_ids": ["C06", "C12"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "6-MNA, a carboxylic acid metabolite, had absolute oral bioavailability of approximately 35–38% in healthy subjects, showing that acidic carboxylate-containing drugs can exceed the 20% threshold.",
      "card_ids": ["C22", "C29"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Bumetanide, an acidic carboxylate/sulfonamide diuretic, showed absolute oral bioavailability values of 0.66–0.95 across healthy-subject studies, indicating that acidic drugs with permeability concerns can still be well absorbed orally.",
      "card_ids": ["C05", "C08", "C10", "C35"]
    }
  ],
